  "rules": [
    "Strong positive level bias in reality vs model: forecasts are consistently too low by ~3–12 EUR, with the gap widening with horizon (small at days 1–3, large by days 10–30). Apply an upward level shift that increases with lead time.",
    "Trend/acceleration underestimation: when the recent history turns up, the model projects flat-to-mild moves while the true path rallies strongly. Add a momentum/acceleration term (e.g., amplify recent 5–10d slope) especially for 1–3 week horizons.",
    "Systematic lag: the model follows the direction but several days late (true prices break higher earlier and stay higher). Pull forward inflection points by ~3–7 days in rising regimes.",
    "Mean-reversion error: the model repeatedly reverts toward ~69–71 even when the market transitions to a higher regime (~75–83). Reduce mean-reversion strength when recent highs are being made; allow regime shift (higher equilibrium) after a breakout.",
    "Horizon-specific correction: minimal adjustment for days 1–3; moderate uplift for days 4–10; large uplift and stronger trend-following for days 11–30 (where underprediction is most severe)."
  ]
}
